  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "In general, the graph of $y={x}^{2}+k$ looks like the standard parabola $y={x}^{2}$ but translated $k$ units up. The vertex of $y={x}^{2}+k$ is located at $(0,k).$\n\nFor the given function $y={x}^{2}+5,$ we have $k=5.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the parabola $y={x}^{2}$ after being translated $5$ units *up*. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218419/assets/a975d014ad92c31850e41367a2b5e46e85ab18a8a7e63bee81cd0f9b6af02bc0.png)\n\nThe vertex is located at $(0,5),$ and these are the coordinates of the minimum point.",
